    "resolved_answer": "$(-7,24)$",
    "resolved_from_fallback": false,
    "final_cot": "Let the implicit function of the line be F(x,y)=3x-2y-a. Substitute the point (-3,-1), obtaining F(-3,-1)=3×(-3)-2×(-1)-a=-9+2-a=-7-a. Substitute the point (4,-6), obtaining F(4,-6)=3×4-2×(-6)-a=12+12-a=24-a. The two points are on two sides of the line 3x-2y-a=0, equivalent to these two function values having opposite signs, so (-7-a)(24-a)<0. After arranging, it can be regarded as -(a+7)(24-a)<0, that is, (a+7)(24-a)>0; therefore a+7>0 and 24-a>0, obtaining -7<a<24.",
